# What `railway up` must NOT upload.
#
# Railway deploys ONE service from this repo: server/api. The upload still has
# to carry the whole workspace, because `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` reads
# every member's package.json and fails on a lockfile whose importers are not
# all present. So this excludes bulk CONTENT, never a package manifest.
#
# apps/web/public alone is 147 MB of photography and hero video. With it in the
# payload the upload timed out before the build ever started; the API needs not
# one byte of it.
apps/web/public
apps/app/public
apps/mobile/assets

# Frontend sources. The API build runs `pnpm --filter @injishi/api build` and
# compiles none of this. The manifests stay, so the workspace still resolves.
apps/web/src
apps/app/src
apps/mobile/app
apps/mobile/src

# Never needed by any build.
.git
docs
